***********************************************************
1. Modifying bits.c and checking it for compliance with dlc
1. 修改 bits.c 并用 dlc 检查合规性
***********************************************************

IMPORTANT: Carefully read the instructions in the bits.c file before
you start. These give the coding rules that you will need to follow if
you want full credit.

重要：开始前请仔细阅读 bits.c 文件中的说明。
其中给出了获取满分所需遵守的编码规则。

Use the dlc compiler (./dlc) to automatically check your version of
bits.c for compliance with the coding guidelines:

使用 dlc 编译器（./dlc）自动检查你的 bits.c 是否符合编码规范：

       unix> ./dlc bits.c

dlc returns silently if there are no problems with your code.
Otherwise it prints messages that flag any problems.  Running dlc with
the -e switch:

如果代码没有问题，dlc 会静默返回。
否则会打印出问题所在的提示信息。
使用 -e 参数运行 dlc：

    	unix> ./dlc -e bits.c  

causes dlc to print counts of the number of operators used by each function.

会让 dlc 打印出每个函数使用的操作数统计。

Once you have a legal solution, you can test it for correctness using
the ./btest program.

在合规的前提下，你可以用 ./btest 程序测试正确性。

*********************
2. Testing with btest
2. 用 btest 测试
*********************

The Makefile in this directory compiles your version of bits.c with
additional code to create a program (or test harness) named btest.

本目录的 Makefile 会把你的 bits.c 和附加代码一起编译，
生成一个名为 btest 的程序（测试工具）。

To compile and run the btest program, type:

编译并运行 btest：

    unix> make btest
    unix> ./btest [optional cmd line args]

You will need to recompile btest each time you change your bits.c
program. When moving from one platform to another, you will want to
get rid of the old version of btest and generate a new one.  Use the
commands:

每次修改 bits.c 后都需要重新编译 btest。
跨平台迁移时，需要删除旧版 btest 并生成新的。
使用以下命令：

    unix> make clean
    unix> make btest

Btest tests your code for correctness by running millions of test
cases on each function.  It tests wide swaths around well known corner
cases such as Tmin and zero for integer puzzles, and zero, inf, and
the boundary between denormalized and normalized numbers for floating
point puzzles. When btest detects an error in one of your functions,
it prints out the test that failed, the incorrect result, and the
expected result, and then terminates the testing for that function.

btest 通过对每个函数运行数百万个测试用例来检查正确性。
它会针对已知的边界情况进行广泛测试：
整数谜题测试 Tmin 和 0 附近的范围，
浮点谜题测试 0、无穷大、
非规格化数与规格化数的边界等。
当 btest 检测到某个函数有错误时，
会打印出失败的测试用例、错误结果和预期结果，
然后终止该函数的测试。

Here are the command line options for btest:

btest 的命令行选项：

  unix> ./btest -h
  Usage: ./btest [-hg] [-r <n>] [-f <name> [-1|-2|-3 <val>]*] [-T <time limit>]
    -1 <val>  Specify first function argument  指定函数第一个参数
    -2 <val>  Specify second function argument 指定函数第二个参数
    -3 <val>  Specify third function argument  指定函数第三个参数
    -f <name> Test only the named function     只测试指定的函数
    -g        Format output for autograding with no error messages
              自动评分格式输出，不带错误信息
    -h        Print this message               打印此帮助信息
    -r <n>    Give uniform weight of n for all problems
              对所有题目给出统一权重 n
    -T <lim>  Set timeout limit to lim         设置超时限制为 lim

Examples:

示例：

  Test all functions for correctness and print out error messages:
  测试所有函数的正确性，打印错误信息：
  unix> ./btest

  Test all functions in a compact form with no error messages:
  以紧凑形式测试所有函数，不打印错误信息：
  unix> ./btest -g

  Test function foo for correctness:
  测试 foo 函数的正确性：
  unix> ./btest -f foo

  Test function foo for correctness with specific arguments:
  用指定参数测试 foo 函数：
  unix> ./btest -f foo -1 27 -2 0xf

Btest does not check your code for compliance with the coding
guidelines.  Use dlc to do that.

btest 不检查代码是否符合编码规范。
请用 dlc 来做这件事。

*******************
3. Helper Programs
3. 辅助程序
*******************

We have included the ishow and fshow programs to help you decipher
integer and floating point representations respectively. Each takes a
single decimal or hex number as an argument. To build them type:

我们提供了 ishow 和 fshow 程序，
分别帮助你理解整数和浮点数的二进制表示。
每个程序接收一个十进制或十六进制数作为参数。
编译命令：

    unix> make

Example usages:

使用示例：

    unix> ./ishow 0x27
    Hex = 0x00000027,	Signed = 39,	Unsigned = 39

    unix> ./ishow 27
    Hex = 0x0000001b,	Signed = 27,	Unsigned = 27

    unix> ./fshow 0x15213243
    Floating point value 3.255334057e-26
    Bit Representation 0x15213243, sign = 0, exponent = 0x2a, fraction = 0x213243
    Normalized.  +1.2593463659 X 2^(-85)

    linux> ./fshow 15213243
    Floating point value 2.131829405e-38
    Bit Representation 0x00e822bb, sign = 0, exponent = 0x01, fraction = 0x6822bb
    Normalized.  +1.8135598898 X 2^(-126)